<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 528 0 R
/E (Preventive maintenance is the only maintenance activity which is carried out without formal maintain an cere quest from the user. When as of ware company or maintain an agency realizes that the methodologies used in a program have )
/Pg 94 0 R
/K [12 13]
>>
endobj
2309 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 528 0 R
/E (Corrective maintenance refers to changes made to repair defects in the design, coding, or implementation of the system. Corrective maintenance is often needed for repairing processing or performance failures or making change because of previously uncorrected problems or false assumptions. Most corrective maintenance problems surface soon after the installation. When corrective maintenance problems surface, they are typically urgent and need to be resolve to curtail possible interruptions in normal business activities. )
/Pg 94 0 R
/K [14 15]
>>
endobj
2310 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 528 0 R
/E (Perfective maintenance involves making enhancements to improve processing performance, interface usability, or to add desired, but not necessarily required, system features. Many system professionals feel that perfective maintenance is not really the maintenance but new development. )
/Pg 94 0 R
/K [16 17]
>>
endobj
2311 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 528 0 R
/E (Adaptive maintenance involves making changes to an information system to evolve its functionality or to migrate it to different operating environment. Adaptive Maintenance is usually less urgent than corrective maintenance because of business and technical changes typically occur some period of time. )
/Pg 94 0 R
/K [18 19]
>>
endobj
